; **The nife terminal font**: an original 7x8 drawing in the style of the Kaypro II's
; character generator. Ours, drawn from scratch; no ROM was traced and no third party's bits
; are here. See notes/glyphs.md for why the ROM itself is excluded and why a style is not.
;
; The geometry is the Kaypro's: a 7-pixel cell of which the middle 5 columns carry ink and the
; outer two are gutter, which is what its video board did in hardware (it shifted out a zero,
; five ROM bits, and a zero). Rows 0-6 are the body, row 7 the descender. Caps and digits fill
; rows 0-6, x-height letters rows 2-6, and the baseline is row 6 for every glyph that has one.
;
; This file is the authoring source and `crates/bitfont/src/glyphs.rs` is generated from it;
; a test in that file parses this back and fails if the two ever disagree. Render it with
;   cargo run -p bitfont --example specimen -- --font crates/bitfont/kaypro-style-7x8.art

